The synonym "Progressive loss of anterior horn cells" can be seen as a rewording of "Degeneration of anterior horn cells." Both terms describe a process involving the deterioration or reduction of anterior horn cells, which are motor neurons located in the spinal cord. The use of "progressive loss" instead of "degeneration" is a minor linguistic variation that does not change the core meaning. Experts in the biomedical field would likely use these terms interchangeably to describe the same pathological process.
